<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nuuk</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Godthåb</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nuuk is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenland">Greenland</a>, on the south-west coast at the mouth of a large fjord system. The missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hans-egede">Hans Egede</a> founded it in 1728 as Godthåb ('good hope'), moving his mission and trading post there, and it became the centre of Danish administration. It officially took the Greenlandic name Nuuk in 1979, when home rule began.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nuuk.jpg" alt="Nuuk" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Quintin Soloviev · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nuuk,_Greenland_skyline_aerial_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
